From 976e488e38be2378a9b7ebe60aae5b14857eeb4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soulexit <metehan.tanriverdi01@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:38:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] pan/bi: Mali-G72 (v6) compiler fixes; kbase fault reports
 per atom

Ported from the jm-v7 series (written for a Galaxy S9, Mali-G72):
- 103: build the v6 ballot from CLPER_OLD instead of WMASK, which is
  not a v6 instruction (INSTR_INVALID_ENC on every compute shader using
  subgroup ballot/vote). This was what blacked out Eden gameplay.
- 095: read_invocation uses the old CLPER encoding on G71/G72/G31.
- 102: pack texture offsets with 32-bit shifts on v6.

kbase: remember each atom's job chain; when an atom fails, walk the chain,
log the job that faulted (decoding instruction-fault addresses) and, with
PANVK_VALIDATE, save the shader that contains the fault next to the driver.

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
